{
    desc => ':s/pat/repl/g substitutes all occurrences on current line',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/ex_substitute_all`

Tests the `:s/old/new/g` ex command which replaces **all** occurrences
of a pattern on the current line (the `g` flag).

**initial.png** — Buffer shows 1 line with "hello" appearing twice.

Keys: `:s/hello/HI/g<Enter>`

**after_substitute_all.png** — Both "hello" instances replaced with "HI".
Line 1 reads `HI world HI again`.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('s/hello/HI/g');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_substitute_all');
    },
}
__DATA__
hello world hello again
